## Requirements

* Python 3.9+
* Nothing else. The standard library is enough to run, test and lint.

## Use

```sh
make run                 # python -m {{ identifier }}
make test                # unittest suite
make lint                # byte-compile every module
make install             # pip install this package
make clean
```

The `make` targets set `PYTHONPATH=src`, so the package is importable without
installing it. To use it directly instead:

```sh
PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m {{ identifier }}
PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t tests
```

## Layout

```
{{ slug }}/
├── Makefile
├── pyproject.toml            src layout, console script '{{ identifier }}'
├── src/{{ identifier }}/
│   ├── __init__.py           public API
│   ├── core.py               framework-free logic
│   ├── cli.py                argparse entry point
│   └── __main__.py           python -m support
└── tests/
    └── test_core.py          unittest suite
```

## Notes

`core.py` deliberately does no I/O, which is what keeps `make test` fast and
dependency-free. Tests use `unittest` rather than pytest on purpose: a
generated project should be testable on a machine with nothing but Python.
